From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:54:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 23/44] minimize: a title without a second row continues on it
 in row 2 style

The wrapped second title line was 14 px at full colour, so it looked
like part of row 1, and a wrap could leave it starting with a space.

Row 1 now takes the longest word-boundary prefix that fits one line
(a character boundary for a single long word), measured with the
renderer's paragraph in the interface font at the available width. A
responsive wrapper supplies that width at layout. The rest, leading
whitespace trimmed, goes into a normal row 2 text: 12 px, 75 % colour,
one line, ellipsized. Both paths share one rows column.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

